   "unmapped": [
    "Arriving user prefers arm a with probability proportional to (S_a(t-1)+theta_a)^alpha_ext (positive externality); non-preferred arms give zero reward, so the arrival process is history-dependent",
    "Regret measured against an Oracle that always pulls a*, whose expected reward is not mu_star*T",
    "Externality exponent alpha_ext and initial popularities theta_a"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "the $t\\kth$ user prefers arm $a$ (i.e., $a\\in J_{t}$) with probability $\\lambda_a(t)$ independently of other arms, where $\\lambda_a(t) = \\frac{f(N_a(t-1))}{\\sum_{a' = 1}^m f(N_{a'}(t-1))}$ ... $R_T = \\Gamma_T^* - \\Gamma_T$."
  },
