   "source": {
    "label": "thm:UCB",
    "number": "Theorem 2",
    "quote": "Suppose $\\gamma > 0$. Suppose that $f(x)$ is $\\Omega\\left(\\ln^{1+\\epsilon}(x)\\right)$ for some $\\epsilon >0$. For UCB($\\gamma$) algorithm, there exists an $\\epsilon' > 0$ such that $$\\mathbb P\\left(\\lim_{T \\to \\infty} {S_{a^*}(T) =0} \\right) \\ge \\epsilon'.$$ In particular, the regret of UCB($\\gamma$) is $O(T)$."
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Paper writes O(T) but means linear regret (Table 1 gives Omega(T)); recorded as Omega(T) lower bound for UCB."
  },
